#DESCRIPTION
Magnetic reconnection (Fadeev current-sheet equilibrium) with the HYBRID
solver (solveEM = F, generalized Ohm's law): kinetic ions / fluid electrons,
companion to PARAM.in.  Reconnection plane x-y, thin invariant z; details in
README.

#INITFROMSWMF
F                       initFromSWMF

#GEOMETRY
-31.4                   xMin  [code units; Lx = 2*pi*L*num_islands ~ 62.8 d_i]
 31.4                   xMax
-15.7                   yMin  [code units; Ly = Lx/2 ~ 31.4 d_i]
 15.7                   yMax
-0.5                    zMin  [thin invariant direction, 1 cell]
 0.5                    zMax

#NCELL
64                      nCellX
32                      nCellY
1                       nCellZ

#MAXBLOCKSIZE
32                      maxBlockSizeX
32                      maxBlockSizeY
1                       maxBlockSizeZ

#PERIODICITY
T                       isPeriodicX
F                       isPeriodicY
T                       isPeriodicZ

Field boundary conditions on the box faces (periodic in x, outflow/float in y,
periodic in z).  The current sheet is far from the y-walls (Ly/2 = 15.7 d_i vs
L = 5 d_i), so a float B boundary reproduces the Hybrid-VPIC PEC cross-sheet
walls closely enough for the interior reconnection.
#BFIELDBOXBOUNDARY
periodic                BoxBoundaryLo  (x)
periodic                BoxBoundaryHi
outflow                 BoxBoundaryLo  (y)
outflow                 BoxBoundaryHi
periodic                BoxBoundaryLo  (z)
periodic                BoxBoundaryHi

#SOLVEEM
F                       solveEM

#HYBRIDPIC
T                       useHybridPIC

Resistive term ON (SI magnetic diffusivity). etaSI = 4.0e5 m^2/s converts to
etaCode ~ 0.001 (as in islands_hyb.cxx).
#RESISTIVITY
4.0e5                   etaResistivity  [m^2/s]

Electron pressure-gradient term ON (isothermal, gamma = 1).
#ELECTRONTEMPERATURE
5.0                     electronTemperature  [eV]
1.0                     electronGamma
1.0                     electronDensity0

Fourth-order hyper-resistivity (mild damping of grid-scale noise).
#HYPERRESISTIVITY
0.0                     etaHyperSI      [m^4/s; unused in grid mode]
grid                    etaHyperMode
0.001                   etaHyperCh

#MINIMUMDENSITY
0.0                     rhoMinOhm

#BSUBCYCLE
1                       nBSubcycle

#FIELDINTEGRATOR
rk4                     fieldIntegrator

#AVGFIELDB
T                       useAvgFieldB
20                      nAvgFieldB

Single kinetic ion species (q = m = 1); the electron is an implicit
neutralizing massless fluid, so no electron particle species is present.
#PLASMA
1                       nSpecies
1.0                     mass
1.0                     charge

#UNIFORMSTATE
12.5                    rho [amu/cc]   background ions (n_code ~ nb = 0.2)
0.0                     ux [km/s]
0.0                     uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
76000.0                 T [K]          ion temperature (beta_i ~ 0.5)
0.0                     bx [T]         guide field set by FadeevIC (bg = 0)
0.0                     by [T]
0.0                     bz [T]
0.0                     ex [V/m]
0.0                     ey [V/m]
0.0                     ez [V/m]

Fadeev current-sheet equilibrium initial condition (see the header description).
#TESTCASE
fadeev

FadeevIC sub-parameters (defaults match islands_hyb.cxx).
#FADEEVIC
5.0                     L        (current-sheet half-thickness / d_i)
0.4                     eps      (island size ratio)
2                       numIslands
1.0                     b0       (reference field, code units)
0.0                     bg       (guide-field ratio; 0 = anti-parallel)
-0.05                   perturb  (m=1 seed amplitude)
0.2                     nb       (background/peak density ratio)

#TIMESTEPPING
T                       useFixedDt
0.02                    dt

#NORMALIZATION
1.0e5                   lNormSI   [m]  ~ d_i so d_i ~ 1 in code units
5.0e4                   uNormSI   [m/s] ~ v_A so v_A ~ 1 in code units

#MONITOR
100                     dnReport

#SAVELOG
10                      dnSavePic
10                      dnSavePT

#PARTICLES
6                       nParticle per cell in X
6                       nParticle per cell in Y
1                       nParticle per cell in Z

#COMOVING
F                       solvePartInCoMov
0                       nSmoothBackGroundU

#UPWINDE
F                       useUpwindE
0.0                     limiterThetaE

#UPWINDB
F                       doSmoothB
0.0                     theta

#SAVEPLOT
1                       nPlot
z=0 fluid ascii pic     plotString
-1                      dn
1.0                     dt
1                       dx
Bx By Bz rhoS0 uxS0 uyS0 uzS0   varName

#STOP
-1                      MaxIter
20.0                    TimeMax

#RUN
